-- title:
--   Answer Eps Le One Of Main Induction Error Lt One
-- statement:
--   **Small main-induction error forces the axis-parallel error below one.**
--
--   Let $S$ be an answer-valued symmetric strategy for the successor parameters, with error parameters $\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma$ and induction index $k$. If $S$ is $(\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma)$-good and
--   `mainInductionError(params.next,k,eps,delta,gamma) < 1`, then
--
--   $$
--   \varepsilon\le1.
--   $$
--
--   This is the answer-valued parameter bound used to justify the hypotheses of the self-improvement error estimate and the small-error successor construction.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MainInductionStep.answer_eps_le_one_of_mainInductionError_lt_one`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
